WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.396
(lights flicker)

00:00:02.396 --> 00:00:03.229
(click)

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.793
(screeching)

00:00:04.793 --> 00:00:05.626
(clumsy music)

00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:08.043
(screeching)

00:00:08.982 --> 00:00:11.232
(growling)

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.483
- Those were big dinosaurs.

00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:14.953
- [Producer] That was a very big dinosaur.

00:00:16.158 --> 00:00:16.991
(happy music)

00:00:16.991 --> 00:00:18.279
- Hey I'm Dee Bra-

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:20.529
(mumbling)

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:23.000
(squeaking)

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:23.833
Take two.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:24.666
(claps)

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:25.980
Hey, I am Dee Bradley Baker.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.300
I'm a voice actor,

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.966
whose known for doing creatures,

00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:29.880
(munching)

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:30.797
monsters,

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.850
(growling)

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.495
and animal sounds in a
lot of Hollywood projects.

00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:38.412
(squeaking sounds)

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.350
My first break probably in voice acting

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.510
would be a Nickelodeon game show called

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.740
"Legends of the Hidden Temple."

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.045
- "Legends of the Hidden Temple,"

00:00:49.045 --> 00:00:51.493
with your guide Kirk Fogg.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:55.050
- I got to do lots of different voices

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.420
as this big rock God Olmec.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.310
I moved his mouth and spoke.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:00.860
- It's my temple.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.530
- That was kind of my first gig

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.010
where it became clear to me

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.936
that I think I wanna
do something like this.

00:01:05.936 --> 00:01:06.800
(click)

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.974
- How about some birds?

00:01:08.974 --> 00:01:10.664
Let's see, turkey?

00:01:10.664 --> 00:01:13.686
(gobbling)

00:01:13.686 --> 00:01:16.728
(cricket chirping)

00:01:16.728 --> 00:01:18.978
(snorting)

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:24.080
(buzzing)

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.610
- When I close off my nose

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:27.560
it gives a resonance to it

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.610
that makes it feel bigger.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.539
For instance,

00:01:30.539 --> 00:01:31.890
(growling)

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:32.723
like that.

00:01:32.723 --> 00:01:33.696
Or,

00:01:33.696 --> 00:01:34.890
(loud growling)

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.940
it's almost like closing off valves

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.330
on a wind instrument,
is how I think of it.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.872
All right, we can wrap it up.

00:01:40.872 --> 00:01:41.740
(laughs)

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.670
I work on all kinds of
different fun shows.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.000
Some of my notable characters might be,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.310
Klaus on American Dad,

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.040
- Hello, Francine, I'm ready

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.070
for my fish feeding now.

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:52.840
- I was Daffy Duck in Space Jam.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.345
All right bub, oy,

00:01:54.345 --> 00:01:56.190
let's make fun of the duck.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.379
- Perry the Platypus in Phineas and Ferb.

00:01:58.379 --> 00:02:00.780
(growling)

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:02.690
A lot of characters in SpongeBob.

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.300
- Squilliam Fancyson and-

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.120
- Perch Perkins Action News.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.811
- And maybe a cop fish.

00:02:07.811 --> 00:02:08.907
There's a fly.

00:02:08.907 --> 00:02:09.740
(buzzing)

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.690
(blows raspberry)

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.857
(buzzing)

00:02:14.811 --> 00:02:15.644
Help me.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.300
I'll get you my pretty.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.255
Where was I?

00:02:19.255 --> 00:02:21.192
(laughs)

00:02:21.192 --> 00:02:22.025
(claps)

00:02:22.025 --> 00:02:23.490
(camera shuttering)

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:24.663
That's a dead fly.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.153
See, if there's anybody else

00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:28.410
that's alive in here.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.290
Now, I'm really into taking pictures of

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:31.720
bugs and small critters.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:32.650
It's a little ant line,

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.400
I think it's eating like aphids off there.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.060
Bugs are like alien robots,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.200
there just, their amazing.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.850
And they have such power

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.980
and such intelligence

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:41.700
and such beauty in their design.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.780
And all of these things

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.526
I find useful to have within me

00:02:44.526 --> 00:02:47.610
for when I'm creating vocal creations.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.760
Here, look at that ant.

00:02:50.256 --> 00:02:51.998
Isn't that beautiful?

00:02:51.998 --> 00:02:53.240
(light music playing)

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.387
Watching biology documentaries,

00:02:55.387 --> 00:02:56.220
(growling)

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.540
the Nature series, Planet Earth series.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.280
I mean those give me all kinds of

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.158
specific ideas in terms of sounds.

00:03:03.158 --> 00:03:05.741
(weird noises)

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.230
- Okay, ready?

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.750
- Ten year old Dee would be impressed

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.150
that middle aged Dee is doing

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.520
creatures and monster sounds

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:15.460
because I loved animals and creatures

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.175
and it looked like a lot of fun.

00:03:17.175 --> 00:03:19.323
- What do you mean?

00:03:19.323 --> 00:03:21.500
- I wanted to put things
out into the world

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:23.200
that make the world better

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.200
and show how interesting and good it is.

00:03:26.065 --> 00:03:29.065
(light piano music)

